//RS     // Shape (d3) [c109 Phase 21 / D-TUPLE-DESTRUCT1]: a Task/Receiver/Sender
//RS     // concurrency method. Sema types these via
//RS     // `Collections::builtin_method_return`'s `Type::Apply` arms
//RS     // (`task_method_return`/`receiver_method_return`/`sender_method_return`,
//RS     // Source/Collections.rs) and leaves `recv_type == None` (a Phase-9 builtin gap).
//RS     // The AST `emit_builtin_method` dispatches them on the method NAME alone
//RS     // (`join`/`detach`/`receive`/`send`). The names + arg counts are disjoint from
//RS     // every other shape: `Task.join()` is the 0-arg `join` (the 1-arg list
//RS     // `join(sep)` is claimed by shape d above); `detach`/`receive` (0 args) and
//RS     // `send` (1 arg) are used by no other builtin. The receiver is a `Task`/
//RS     // `Receiver`/`Sender` value `(tx, rx) := tasks.channel<T>()`-destructured or
