//RS     // Shape (d4): `Match.group(n)` (D-REGEXENGINE1). Sema sets `recv_type ==
//RS     // Some("Match")` (the `Match` receiver type, CheckerInfer's user/handle-method
//RS     // writeback), and the AST `emit_builtin_method` dispatches it on the method NAME
//RS     // guarded by `rty == Some(Named("Match"))` (Expression.rs ~L1132). Keyed on
//RS     // `recv_type == Some("Match")` + `group`/1 — disjoint from every user instance method
//RS     // (whose `recv_type` is a covered struct/enum, never `Match`) and from the numeric
//RS     // shape (a numeric `recv_type`). The receiver is a `Match` value (`if m == value(mat)`
