//RS /// c109 Phase 7: is a STATIC method call `Type.make(args)` inside the subset? The
//RS /// AST path (Expression.rs ~L1644) emits `__jet_<Type>::__jet_<method>(args)` for a
//RS /// `MethodCall` whose receiver is an ident in `cx.type_names`. We admit exactly that
//RS /// case, conservatively:
//RS ///   - `type_name` is NOT a local (a local shadowing a type would be a field/method
//RS ///     access, not a static call);
//RS ///   - `type_name` is a covered struct or enum (so its `__jet_<T>` prefix is right);
//RS ///   - `method` is NOT an enum *variant* of `type_name` — a `Enum.Variant(args)`
//RS ///     receiver+method emits an enum literal (a different lowering, Expression.rs
//RS ///     ~L1635), so exclude it (Phase 4 covers enum literals via `Expr::EnumLit`/
//RS ///     unit `Expr::Field`, not this MethodCall shape);
//RS ///   - `method` is NOT a builtin/special intercept (`new`, etc.);
//RS ///   - `(type_name, method)` is a registered user method (`method_sigs`);
//RS ///   - every arg is in-subset, unlabeled, and not Fn-typed.
//RS /// D-PROTO1/D-PROTO2: resolve a static-method receiver to a user type name.
//RS /// `Payment.Client.client()` is `MethodCall(Field(Ident(Payment), Client), …)`.
